# CODEOWNERS — cross-team file-ownership boundary (seed K.10, Pipeline v2.1 Day-1 baseline)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# When the app team and DevOps share one repo, the files DevOps customizes for the
# production build/deploy (Dockerfile, /deploy/**, CI/CD config) are a cross-TEAM
# contract surface. A feature branch carrying its own copy of these files will silently
# overwrite DevOps's customizations on merge, and the next CI build ships the wrong
# image (the EF-AI S34 "deployed pod still ran the old code" hour). Marking the boundary
# here means GitHub auto-requests the owning team's review on any PR that touches them,
# and (with branch protection "Require review from Code Owners") can require their
# approval before merge.
#
# SETUP (Stage 0):
#   1. Replace <DEVOPS_HANDLE> with the real team/user, e.g. @your-org/devops.
#      The owner MUST have write access to the repo (GitHub requirement).
#   2. In repo Settings -> Branches (or a ruleset), enable
#      "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch.
#   3. If this is a solo / no-DevOps repo, delete the build/deploy lines below
#      rather than leaving a fake owner — an unmatched/invalid owner assigns no one.
#
# SYNTAX: <path-pattern>  <owner1> [owner2 ...]  (last matching pattern wins)
# Paths are case-sensitive. `!` negation and `[ ]` ranges are NOT supported here.

# ---- W-021 RULED AND CLOSED, 2026-08-17 (M6 closure, owner's decision) ----
# This file used to carry six rules assigning `/Dockerfile`, `/.dockerignore`, `/deploy/`,
# `/.github/workflows/`, `/Makefile` and this file itself to `<DEVOPS_HANDLE>`.
#
# `<DEVOPS_HANDLE>` is not a GitHub handle. Every rule matched its pattern and requested review
# from no one, and that had been true since Stage 0 — a control that read as installed and was
# inert. M6-W4 made it matter by creating the first files those rules pointed at (`Dockerfile`,
# `fly.toml`), and M6 found the same class of defect four separate times, so leaving a sixth
# standing at the closing gate was not defensible.
#
# **The owner ruled: delete the rules.** This is a solo repository with no DevOps team, which is
# the case the SETUP note above already prescribes deletion for — an unmatched or invalid owner
# assigns no one, so a rule naming a placeholder is advisory fiction that reads as a boundary.
# The alternative (a real handle PLUS "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch)
# was rejected as describing a review that no second person exists to perform.
#
# **K.10's boundary is not abandoned, it is relocated to where it is actually enforced:**
# AGENTS.md §5 forbids agents overwriting DevOps-owned build/deploy files, and
# `conformance/test-governed-paths.py` checks the governed globs. Those run. This file did not.
#
# If a second contributor or a DevOps team ever joins, restore the rules with a real handle AND
# enable the branch-protection setting in the same change — the file is advisory without it.

